INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Selection <strong>Drip tape spacing in mung bean cultivation</strong> This is a major challenge for farmers and irrigation engineers, directly affecting irrigation efficiency and crop quality. Mung bean, a legume crop with a shallow root system and high sensitivity to water stress during seed fill, requires the intelligent management of drip irrigation systems. In this guide, we cover all technical aspects, from spacing theory to field operations, enabling you to confidently adjust your drip tape layout.</p><h2>Introduction to the Importance of Drip Tape Layout in Mung Bean</h2><p>Drip tape systems have gained significant popularity due to their lower cost compared to permanent drip systems and their ability to be collected and recycled after the end of the cropping season. However, this system requires high precision in the distance of tapes from the row center and the spacing between adjacent tapes. The primary goal is to create a coherent wetted front that encompasses the mung bean root zone. If the spacing between tapes is too wide, resulting dry gaps will cause water stress during the pod fill stage. If the spacing is too narrow, water is wasted in non-root zones, increasing system costs.</p><h2>Technical Standards for Drip Tape Spacing in Mung Bean</h2><p>Determining the precise drip tape spacing depends on variables such as soil type, mung bean root depth, and solar radiation intensity. Nevertheless, general standards for temperate and semi-arid regions of Iran are as follows:</p><ul><li><strong>Distance of tape from row center:</strong> A spacing of 5 to 10 cm is generally recommended. A 10 cm distance is ideal for better seed germination and prevention of stem fungal diseases in high humidity near the base of the plant. Spacings of less than 5 cm may cause plant death due to root asphyxiation in clay soils.</li><li><strong>Single-line vs. dual-line configuration:</strong> For cabbage rows spaced 60 to 70 cm apart, using a single drip line in the center or two lateral lines spaced 10–15 cm from the row center is more common. In a dual-line system, the distance between the two lines should be such that the wet zones of the two lines almost touch each other.</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><th>Soil type</th><th>Recommended line spacing from row center</th><th>Description</th></tr><tr><td>Sandy and light soils</td><td>15–20 cm</td><td>Coarse soil texture requires wetting a larger root volume; place the drip lines farther from the center.</td></tr><tr><td>Loamy and medium soils</td><td>8–12 cm</td><td>The most balanced condition; the industry standard in most farms in Iran.</td></tr><tr><td>Clayey and heavy soils</td><td>4–6 cm</td><td>To prevent waterlogging and root rot, keep the drip line close to the trunk.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For a better understanding of how water moves through soil, review the study on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%AC%D9%88-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%B1-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Barley and mustard yield per hectare</a> It can clarify the similarities and differences in irrigating bush and seed crops. Although mung bean is a seed crop, its root behavior shares similarities with vegetables and other seed crops, as analyzed in the link above.</p><h3>Practical Installation and Maintenance Tips</h3><p>Proper spacing execution should not remain on paper. In practice, using precision furrowers or guide strips helps you control the deviation of the strip from the center along the row. After planting and before the initial watering, ensure the drip tape is lying on the soil without kinking. Kinking alters flow velocity and creates weak points in the strip over the long term.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-ماش-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت ماش: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop mung bean</figcaption></figure><p>Note that the drip tape spacing for beans may vary slightly, as beans differ from mung beans in fine details regarding root structure and water requirements. However, the general principles of drip tape spacing management for bush vegetables are shared and can serve as a good guide for other crops.</p><h2>Pressure Management and Manifold Line Design</h2><p>Aligning drip tape spacing is linked to the correct design of the manifold network. If manifold lines flow in parallel and at the same pressure, water distribution along the strip will be uniform. Otherwise, the end section of the strip will be dry and the initial section will be wet, causing asymmetric mung bean growth in the row.</p><ol><li><strong>Pressure drop calculation:</strong> As the field length increases, pressure at the end of the mainline decreases. To compensate, increase the diameter of the mainline pipe or design shorter parallel lines.</li><li><strong>Strip tube perforation:</strong> Modern strip tubes feature emitters with a flow rate of 27 liters per hour. This rate is suitable for rice at the vegetative stage, but you may need to increase water volume during the grain-filling stage. In this case, do not change the strip spacing; instead, adjust the irrigation duration.</li></ol><p>For details on strip tube specifications and suitable strips for salt-sensitive plants and drainage, you can refer to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/nuqtahoi-muhim-hangomi-istifodai-lundahoi-tipisi-baroi-obyori/">Key points when using strip tubes for irrigation</a> for reference. This guide also covers the polymer properties of the strips and their resistance to UV radiation.</p><h2>Impact of strip spacing on yield quality and quantity</h2><p>Research has shown that optimizing <strong>drip tape spacing in mung bean cultivation</strong> can save up to 15 percent in water usage while maintaining or even increasing yield per hectare. When the tape spacing is optimal, roots fully cover the wetted zone created by the tape, eliminating the need to search for water at deeper, non-wetted levels. This directs plant energy toward flowering and pod development instead of producing fine root hairs.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-ماش-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت ماش: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop mung bean</figcaption></figure><p>Additionally, selecting an appropriate spacing allows for more precise fertilization (Fertigation). If the tapes are too far apart, nitrogenous fertilizers will leach due to their high mobility. If they are too close, the accumulation of nutrients in a single spot can cause root burn in mung beans. Balancing the drip tape spacing creates a path for safe and effective fertilization.</p><p>In farms practicing intercropping, or if you are using drip tapes for other vegetables such as lettuce or cucumber, familiarizing yourself with other spacings helps you understand general patterns. For example, a study <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/lula-3-dyimmagi-kharid-istifoda-imkoniyathoi/">the availability of purchasing and using 3-millimeter drip tape</a> indicates that using thicker tapes (such as 4 or 5 millimeters) in double-sided rows can increase the functional life of the tape and minimize concerns about tape breakage.</p><h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3>1. Is it possible to change the tape spacing after planting?</h3><p>No, changing the tape distance from the row center after planting is practically impossible, as the tape must be positioned directly under the shade canopy and within the root zone. Therefore, this decision must be specified and fixed on the planting map before sowing.</p><h3>2. What is the standard spacing for sandy soils?</h3><p>Due to the high permeability of sandy soil, the tapes should be placed farther from the row center (approximately 15–20 centimeters) to create a wider wetted volume and prevent rapid water loss.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-ماش-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت ماش: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop ماش</figcaption></figure><h3>3. What is the role of water salinity in drip tape spacing?</h3><p>For saline water, engineers typically recommend using tapes with a higher flow rate and maintaining the same physical spacing, while applying a higher volume of water for leaching at the end of the season. The physical distance of the tape from the stem does not fundamentally change in these conditions, but the system flow rate is adjusted.</p><h2>Summary and Final Recommendations</h2><p>Optimization <strong>Drip tape spacing for mung bean cultivation</strong> This is a data-driven process. You must integrate soil science, mung bean cultivar type, and regional climatic conditions. Starting from standard averages (approximately 10 centimeters in medium-textured soils) and then adjusting the spacing based on actual soil moisture measurements (using a tensiometer or the squeeze test) is the most reliable path to success.</p><p>Attention to maintenance and extending system lifespan is also critical. To learn about methods for preventing emitter clogging and increasing the service life of drip systems, you can read the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/afzaliyathoi-lentai-qatragi/">Increasing Efficiency in Drip Tape Irrigation Systems</a> . These tips will help you maintain your irrigation system investment for future years and avoid early replacement costs for the tapes.</p><p>Ultimately, a well-configured drip tape system increases the economic efficiency of mung bean planting by reducing water, energy, and labor costs while preserving field texture for subsequent crops. You can also study the more successful experiences of farmers using laid pipelines for large farms. <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%b7-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%aa%d9%86%d9%82%d9%8a%d8%b7-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%aa%da%a9%d8%b1%db%8c%d8%aa/">Drip irrigation tapes in terms of definitions and advanced solutions</a> Take note: although this source is a mixed Persian/Arabic reference, the principles of the drip line system are fully applicable to Iranian farms.</p>','Tipe Strip Spacing in Mung Bean Cropping: Recommended Standards','This article examines the optimal strip line spacing for mung bean cultivation, recommended standards based on soil type and irrigation system, and key practical tips for improving drip line performance.','publish','closed','closed','tipe-strip-spacing-mung-bean-cropping-recommended-standards',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
